      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and it carries a real risk of serious harm to the patient. You've also said you aren't a clinician, so this dose hasn't had prescriber review.\n\nHere are some ways to go forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the safe range.** Tell me the dose and I'll enter it right away. For example, ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth three times daily is 2,400 mg/day. Ibuprofen 800 mg four times daily is 3,200 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **Ask the treating prescriber to place the order.** If they believe a higher dose is warranted, they can enter it directly and consult pharmacy. They would be accountable for that decision.\n- **Ask pharmacy to clarify.** They can help work out what was intended, for example if 1,600 mg was meant as a total daily dose.\n\nI'm glad to enter a corrected order as soon as you have a dose."
      }
